Slice 079: `fx/units` has one row (the app `acme/old` fails its check with each compiler) and `fx/hooks` counts one `probes` call more for each run after run 6 (the check of the try is a `probes` call), so its numbers are 4 and 5.

Slice 079b (R-T30, R-SO10, Q3 of slice 079): the selected compiler of a tool command is also the `roc` on `PATH` when ranks 2 (`ROC_TOOLCHAIN`) and 6 (`default-roc`) give nothing and its id is a nightly or a release (rank 7). It is looked up only then, so each run with no default and no `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` that chooses a compiler has the call `path_roc` (and the calls of slice 022b the first time) before the choice. The `PATH` has no `roc`: one `path_roc` call in the runs 6 and 7 and the run 8 (no default is set before run 7). Slice 080 (R-SO24, R-SO6): with no `default-roc` the newest installed nightly or release is rank 6, so one `list_dirs` of `<cache>/toolchains` comes first (`ToolFlow.selected_for!`), and the `path_roc` lookup (rank 7) only when nothing is installed.
